Expected elements: REPLACED — "A timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace" by the bare `128 / 1315` fraction readout in the identity bar

Every other must-show item is present and recognisable: the provenance banner above the bar, the exit to `aztec`, `0xb63616…6359`, `Partial`, `block 101`, four stepping pairs carrying both directions, the FETCHING/OPENING/POSITIONING rail, a Code pane positioned unmistakably at line 32, Call Trace and Event Log as one tab strip with Call Trace open, Values as a pane below it, and the Transaction pane's identity. Nothing forbidden appears. But no graphical time surface renders at this width — the 48-tick scrubber is suppressed below 1780px, and a fraction is a readout, which the backbone already requires separately. That is finding 1, P1, and it caps the rating at 4.

The type system is otherwise disciplined and genuinely dense. What holds it back is that it has three digit-grouping conventions (`1,315` in the ACIR column, `1315` in the readout, `88000` in COST · MANA), two hash strategies inside one pane (middle-ellipsis in the Transaction header, three-line wraps ending in two-character orphans below it), double truncation on deep Call Trace rows, and one uppercase letterspaced treatment doing pane title, group heading and field label alike. The banner's prose is the largest, loosest text in the shell.

Highest-priority fixes: restore a time surface at 1440; give digits and hashes one rule each.

Rating: 4/10

